<title>DENMARK: Danish FLS wins STG 25 mln BA order.</title>
<headline>Danish FLS wins STG 25 mln BA order.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish group FLS Industries' British-based unit FLS Aerospace Ltd has won a contract to supply aircraft engineering services to British Airways, worth 25 million pounds over three years, a statement from the parent company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said that the deal, covering Gatwick, Manchester and Stansted aiprorts from next month until October 2000, would allow FLS Aerospace to reopen its Gatwick hangar, closed for the past four years for lack of business.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
